,title,link,text,language,family
0,Xingu Asurini language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xingu_Asurini_language,"Xingú Asuriní (Asurini of Xingu) is a Tupi–Guaraní language of the state of Pará, in the Amazon region of Brazil. The entire population speaks the language, and most speakers are monolingual.",Asurini of Xingú,Tupian
1,Asurini of Xingú - asn (Tupian) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/asn/,"Asurini of Xingú (asn) is part of the Tupian family and Tupian, Tupí-Guaraní, Kayabí class. Asurini of Xingú speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts: Types.",Asurini of Xingú,Tupian
2,Endangered Languages Project - Asuriní of Xingú,https://elcat.colo.hawaii.edu/lang/678,"Asuriní de coatinema, Asurini do Xingu, Asuriní do Koatinema, Awaeté, Xingú Asuriní, Assurinikin. CLASSIFICATION. Tupian, Tupi-Guaranian, Xingu. Code authority. Iso 639-3.",Asurini of Xingú,Tupian
3,Ritual Music of Asurini & Arara Indians - Amazon.com Music,https://www.amazon.com/Ritual-Music-Asurini-Arara-Indians/dp/B000007XO9,"Ritual Music of Asurini & Arara Indians.""Enregistrements (Brésil, 1987, 1989 et 1990), texte de présentation et photographies : Jean-Pierre Estival. La pièce n°7 a été enregistrée par les Asurini do Xingu, avec l'aide des Irmãzinhas de Jesus et Lucia Andrade.",Asurini of Xingú,Tupian
4,Asurini do Xingu - Indigenous Peoples in Brazil,https://pib.socioambiental.org/en/Povo:Asurini_do_Xingu,"Asurini material culture includes the following items: ceramics, weaving, basketry, weapons, body ornaments, wooden benches and musical instruments (flutes). Ceramics and weaving (hammocks, slings, headbands and other ornaments made of cotton) are the women’s tasks.",Asurini of Xingú,Tupian
5,Glottolog 5.3 - Xingú Asuriní,https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/xing1248,"Asuriní of Xingú (678-asn) = Endangered (20 percent certain, based on the evidence available) [ed. 2010](cldf:ed:10).Asurini do Xingu. Asuriní de coatinema. Asuriní do Koatinema. Asuriní of Xingú.",Asurini of Xingú,Tupian
6,Awaete Language and the Awaeté Indian Tribe (Asurini do Xingu...),https://www.native-languages.org/awaete.htm,"Awaete Indian Language (Asurini do Xingu, Awaeté). Language: Awaeté is a Tupian language of South America. It is an agglutinative language with fairly free word order. Awaete is spoken by around 200 people in Brazil.",Asurini of Xingú,Tupian
7,Asuriní of Xingú language information,https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/AsuriniofXingu,"Alternate names: Asuriní de coatinema, Asurini do Xingu, Asuriní do Koatinema, Awaeté, Xingú Asuriní, Assurinikin. Language code: asn. Language family: Tupian, Tupí-Guaraní, Kayabí (SIL classification). Number of speakers: Vulnerability: Dormant.",Asurini of Xingú,Tupian
8,Asurini of Xingu language resources | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/index.php/languages/asn,Listing of people groups speaking Asurini of Xingu. Asurini of Xingu dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability.,Asurini of Xingú,Tupian
9,Category:Xingú Asuriní terms derived from Tupian languages...,https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Category:Xingú_Asuriní_terms_derived_from_Tupian_languages,"Xingú Asuriní terms that originate from one of the Tupian languages. This category should, ideally, contain only other categories. Entries can be categorized here, too, when the proper subcategory is unclear.",Asurini of Xingú,Tupian
